@*
    Audit Configuration flow (migration 276) -- Phase 1.

    Screen key : `org-audit-configuration`
    Group      : Audit Management
    Menu       : nav-assurance ("Audit Management") -> Audit Configuration
                 (a clickable parent: a real page AND the parent of the
                 five screens it hosts)

    How the audit operates, once it is defined:
        543: Scope Builder -> org-assurance-scope-builder
             Question Sets -> _audit-question-set-adoption
             (moved here from Audit Definition, which keeps only details)
        1. Workflow Configuration -> org-assurance-workflow-config
        2. Scoring Configuration  -> org-assurance-scoring-config
        (548: Trigger is no longer a step -- executions start from plan
        slots; 545: Scope Resolution is the Scope Builder's Preview.)
    (Evidence Configuration was step 1 until 536 removed it: the
    evidence an audit collects is set per question -- Evidence Type and
    Expected Evidence -- in its Question Sets.)

    ORDER, AND WHY
      All five are keyed on (org_assurance_definition_id,
      org_assurance_definition_version_id), so they share one audit
      context and the first four are independent of each other -- the
      order is the BRD reading order (Sec 5, 6, 7, 9), not a dependency
      chain. Scope Resolution is last on purpose: it RESOLVES the scope
      authored in the Audit Definition flow into a snapshot, so it is
      the step that is meaningful only once the rest is in place. Its
      snapshots are immutable, which makes it the natural closing
      review step.

    537 (2026-11-13, sir): THE PAGE IS A LIST NOW
      The page opens on the list of audits to configure (Draft, scope and
      question sets set), one Organization picker; 3-dot / row click ->
      the audit's view -> Actions -> a step. The steps below are hosted by
      the flow shell in hosted mode (no context bar, no URL ids) inside
      Partials/_audit-configuration-workspace, which drives it.

    545 (2026-11-13, sir): FIVE STEPS. Scope Resolution is no longer a
      step: the scope is resolved when an execution is created
      (sp_org_assurance_execution_materialize). Its screen stays as the
      Preview under the Scope Builder (Partials/_audit-scope-step).
      562 (2026-11-15): the Preview is replaced by Step 2, Discover Related
      GRAC Intelligence; Step 1 picks the audit subjects (Operationalize
      dependencies).

    543 (2026-11-13, sir): SIX STEPS, ONE POPUP EACH
      Scope Builder and Question Sets are the first two steps (Scope
      Resolution resolves that scope, so it needs it). The view page's
      step list is where an audit is configured: a step row opens that
      step alone in a popup with its own Save; saving marks the step
      Completed. The one-page sections and the single Save are gone.

    564 (2026-11-15, sir): Control and Practice Mapping is a step between
      the Scope Builder and Question Sets (Partials/_audit-mapping-step).
      It is OPTIONAL (status Optional until something is mapped) and never
      blocks Submit for Review.

    ASSURANCE PLANS IS DELIBERATELY NOT A STEP HERE
      org_assurance_plan is organization-scoped and its items each
      reference a definition, so one plan spans several audits. Nesting
      it inside a per-audit stepper would invert that relationship, so
      it stays its own item under Audit Management.
*@
@model PracticeManagement.Web.Models.PracticeScreen
@{
    var flow = new AuditFlowShell(Model, "oaAuditConfigurationFlow",
    new AuditFlowStep[]
    {
        // 543: keys and titles match fn_org_assurance_setup_steps
        // (StepKey / StepName), which the step list is built from.
        // 545: the Scope Builder with a Preview (the Scope Resolution
        // screen) under it -- Scope Resolution is no longer a step.
        new AuditFlowStep(
            "scope",
            "Scope Builder",
            "Step 1: the audit subjects (Operationalize dependencies). Step 2: the related GRAC intelligence they lead to.",
            "Partials/_audit-scope-step"),
        // 564: Control and Practice Mapping (spec 4.2.2) -- optional;
        // between the scope and the question sets, the spec's order.
        new AuditFlowStep(
            "mapping",
            "Control and Practice Mapping",
            "Optional: the controls, practices and practice instances this audit is about, and manual mappings. Context only.",
            "Partials/_audit-mapping-step"),
        new AuditFlowStep(
            "questions",
            "Question Sets",
            "Which question sets this audit asks, in order. New sets are made in Audit > Question Sets.",
            "Partials/_audit-question-set-adoption"),
        new AuditFlowStep(
            "workflow",
            "Workflow",
            "The stages the audit moves through, who owns each one, and the SLA.",
            "Partials/org-assurance-workflow-config"),
        new AuditFlowStep(
            "scoring",
            "Scoring",
            "How results are scored: model type, thresholds and outcome bands.",
            "Partials/org-assurance-scoring-config")
        // 548 (sir): the Trigger step is removed -- nothing runs an audit
        // from a trigger; executions start from plan slots (546).
    }, Hosted: true);
}

<partial name="Partials/_audit-configuration-workspace" model="flow" />
